course: dictionary
lesson: 14664
title: Prehistory: the time before writing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Prehistory is the very long time in the past before people wrote things down. Because nobody wrote anything then, we cannot read about it in books. Instead, we learn about it from things people left behind, such as tools, bones and cave paintings.
explain: Break the word into parts to check it. Pre means before, and history means the recorded past. So prehistory is the time before written history. «Long ago, in prehistory, people made tools from flint.» The clues are "long ago" and "made tools", not writing.
explain: The word has a second meaning too. You can talk about the prehistory of something, meaning its early beginnings. «The prehistory of computers includes early ideas that came long before the first machines.»
fact: Prehistory means the time before people wrote things down.
fact: Archaeologists and historians learn about prehistory from tools, bones, pots and cave paintings.
fact: The Stone Age, the Bronze Age and the Iron Age are all part of prehistory.
fact: Stonehenge and Skara Brae are famous places that help us study prehistory.
fact: Dinosaurs lived long before any humans, in the much older past of the Earth.
exercise: «Scientists learn about prehistory from bones and tools that people left behind.» What is prehistory? | A lesson about writing and spelling | A type of school book | The future, after the year 3000 | *The time before people wrote things down
exercise: Which of these is part of prehistory? | *The Stone Age | Today's news | The Internet | The Tudors
exercise: «The museum showed the prehistory of the car, from early ideas to the first engines.» What does prehistory mean here? | Cars sold in shops this year | A story about a racing driver | *The early beginnings of cars | A car park full of old cars
test: Why can we learn about prehistory from cave paintings but not from books? | Cave paintings are found inside books | Books are too heavy to carry | *Nobody had written things down yet | Cave paintings are too new to study
test: Which word means the very long time before writing? | Mystery | *Prehistory | Geography | History
exam: «Archaeologists study Skara Brae to learn about prehistory.» What helps them learn most about prehistory? | Modern newspapers | Their own memories of the village | A diary written by the villagers | *Things people left behind, such as tools and bones
